<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joyous Entry of 1356</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1356</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Blijde Inkomst, Joyous Entry</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Joyous Entry was a charter of liberties granted in January 1356 by Duchess Joanna and Duke Wenceslaus to the estates of Brabant in return for recognition of their rule. It limited the duke's power to wage war, coin money and appoint foreigners to office, and allowed subjects to refuse obedience if their rights were broken. Sworn by every later ruler, it was invoked in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a> against Philip II.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joyous-entry-of-1356.jpg" alt="Joyous Entry of 1356" width="320" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: nl:Johanna van Brabant en Wenceslas. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blijde_Inkomst.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
